# =============================================================================
# {{PROJECT}} — environment contract for THIS PROJECT'S OWN APP STACK
# =============================================================================
# Every key the app needs appears here, with NO real values. This file is
# committed; `.env` is not (see .gitignore) and is never read or printed by an
# agent.
#
# It is also mounted OVER /repo/.env inside the fleet's container, so what the
# agents see when they open the app's `.env` is exactly this — fake. That is
# deliberate: a rule an agent is asked to follow is a request, a mount is a
# fact.
#
# The Warden dev-fleet (the agents that BUILD this project) has its own,
# separate env at deploy/warden/.env — GH_TOKEN, MAX_CONCURRENT and the rest
# of the fleet's variables live there, not here. This file is only for the
# app deploy/docker-compose.yml itself will read once it is authored
# (MANIFEST.md — that file is authored per-project, not part of the kit).
# =============================================================================

# This project's published-port block, bound to 127.0.0.1. Pick a free block and
# check it is actually free (`lsof -iTCP:<port> -sTCP:LISTEN`) — 5432, 6379,
# 3000 and 8080 are taken on any machine already running one other project.
HOST_PORT_BASE=

# Add the rest of this app's own variables here as deploy/docker-compose.yml
# grows to need them.
